title: What I learned in my first month
from: Wren talks
gist: You gave a small talk on the auditorium stage about your first month aboard.
== lines
calder > you: You're on, {me}. Ring of chairs, tea's there. Take as long as you like. Not too long.   [nod]
torres-zeke: Go on! We're all friends here. Mostly Works, but friends.   [laugh]
? choice
* (Talk about the first job you fixed)   rel:calder+2 flavour:practical
  calder: Good. You told it straight, including the bit you got wrong. That's the best part of any talk.   [nod]
* (Talk about the crew who helped)   rel:torres-zeke+2 flavour:share
  torres-zeke: You named everyone. Even me. I'm not crying. It's the tea.   [laugh]
* (Talk about the stars from the observatory)   flavour:listen
  tomas: That was lovely. I'm going to look up properly next time.   [nod]
calder: Thank you, {me}. That's the first month done properly.
